      "id": 483679,
      "username": "pvanthony",
      "name": "P V Anthony",
      "created_at": "2025-10-11T05:21:39.037Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Thank you for the advice. Very helpful.</p>\n<p>From the erpnext telegram chat Devel Biene shared the following link.</p><aside class=\"quote\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"14032\">\n  <div class=\"title\">\n    <div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n    <img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/rwema_aimable/48/28198_2.png\" class=\"avatar\">\n    <a href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/t/passing-argument-to-bench-execute/14032\">Passing argument to bench execute</a> <a class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/framework/app-development/24\"><span data-category-id=\"24\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #0E76BD; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF; --parent-category-badge-color: #F7941D;\" data-parent-category-id=\"5\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category --has-parent\"><span class=\"badge-category__name\">App Development</span></span></a>\n  </div>\n  <blockquote>\n    Hello, is it possible to call a function that expects arguments with bench execute?\n  </blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>\nWhich was also helpful.</p>\n<p>Here is what worked for me on erpnext 15.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">bench --site erpnext.domain.com execute app_name.pvtest.my_function\n</code></pre>\n<p>Please note the following.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the script file was placed in app_name/app_name</li>\n<li>file name is pvtest.py</li>\n<li>the function name in the file pvtest.py is called my_function.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>So even if the script was in app_name/app_name, we only call it with one app_name instead of app_name.app_name.</p>",
